   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Synthetic process data for digital twins with SDV and NeqSim\n",
    "\n",
    "Synthetic data imitate selected statistical and engineering behaviour without copying\n",
    "individual plant records. This notebook combines two complementary approaches:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. SDV learns multivariate and sequential patterns from a compact process-history table.\n",
    "2. NeqSim supplies thermodynamically consistent TEG-dehydration responses for operating\n",
    "   scenarios sampled from that table.\n",
    "\n",
    "Synthetic data are useful for software tests, operator training and early model\n",
    "development when measured data are sparse or sensitive. They are not automatically\n",
    "anonymous, physically valid or suitable for design. Every generated scenario therefore\n",
    "needs statistical quality checks, domain checks and, when used for engineering decisions,\n",
    "a first-principles confirmation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "696d4a9e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Learning objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "After completing the notebook, you can:\n",
    "\n",
    "- define SDV metadata for process time series and train a PAR synthesizer;\n",
    "- compare real and synthetic marginal distributions and temporal behaviour;\n",
    "- generate a conditioned high-water scenario with a supported SDV synthesizer;\n",
    "- map sampled process variables into a reusable NeqSim `ProcessSystem`;\n",
    "- retrieve dehydration, regeneration and balance results with explicit units; and\n",
    "- screen a lean-TEG sensitivity and reject results that fail physical checks."
   ]
  },
