   "source": [
    "## Synthetic data generation for gas-process digital twins\n",
    "\n",
    "**Training.** A statistical learner can be trained on synthetic rows generated by a\n",
    "validated process model or on a privacy-reviewed operational table.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Testing and validation.** Controlled scenarios expose how a digital twin responds to\n",
    "high water, changing throughput and altered solvent circulation.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Privacy and security.** Synthetic values can reduce disclosure risk, but resemblance to\n",
    "training records must still be measured. This tutorial uses a deterministic,\n",
    "non-proprietary fallback rather than requiring private plant history.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Engineering consistency.** SDV reproduces statistical patterns; NeqSim evaluates the\n",
    "phase behaviour and connected equipment. Agreement with the training distribution does\n",
    "not prove conservation or thermodynamic feasibility."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "99d1f351",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## The Synthetic Data Vault\n",
    "\n",
    "The Synthetic Data Vault (SDV) is a Python library for tabular, relational and sequential\n",
    "synthetic data. Metadata describe column semantics, while a synthesizer learns and samples\n",
    "the joint distribution. This notebook uses:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `PARSynthesizer` for ordered sequences;\n",
    "- `GaussianCopulaSynthesizer` for conditional and independent-row demonstrations; and\n",
    "- SDV quality metrics plus explicit process-domain checks."
   ]
  },
