    "## Synthetic data generation in four steps\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Prepare data and metadata.\n",
    "2. Fit a synthesizer.\n",
    "3. Generate sequential or conditioned synthetic data.\n",
    "4. evaluate statistical quality and engineering validity.\n",
    "\n",
    "The final NeqSim section adds a fifth practical step: confirm that selected scenarios are\n",
    "thermodynamically and operationally plausible."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dce8d5d5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Prepare a process-history table\n",
    "\n",
    "The original notebook read `TimeSeries.csv` from this repository. That public source\n",
    "remains documented and can be enabled below. The default is a deterministic fallback with\n",
    "the same key tags and units so that notebook execution never depends on raw-file hosting.\n",
    "It represents four synthetic operating campaigns sampled every 30 minutes.\n",
    "\n",
    "The retained signals are:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `AIT-1x34.PV` and `AIT-1x35.PV`: water-analyser readings, ppm(mol);\n",
    "- `STN1x-FT.INUSE2`: gas-rate indicator, scaled standard-flow signal;\n",
    "- `FIT-1xx2.`: lean-TEG circulation, kg/h; and\n",
    "- `PIT-xxx9.`: gas pressure, bara."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "c580dd24",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Data resolution: deterministic documented fallback\n",
      "Raw rows: 192\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from io import BytesIO\n",
    "from urllib.request import urlopen\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_URL = (\n",
    "    \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EvenSol/NeqSim-Colab/\"\n",
    "    \"master/notebooks/process/TimeSeries.csv\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "USE_REMOTE_REPOSITORY_DATA = False\n",
    "RANDOM_SEED = 42\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def build_deterministic_process_history():\n",
    "    rng = np.random.default_rng(RANDOM_SEED)\n",
    "    campaigns = [\"ASTERIX\", \"OBELIX\", \"IDEFIX\", \"PANORAMIX\"]\n",
    "    frames = []\n",
    "\n",
    "    for campaign_number, campaign_name in enumerate(campaigns):\n",
    "        step = np.arange(48, dtype=float)\n",
    "        phase = campaign_number * 0.65\n",
    "        load_wave = np.sin(step / 7.0 + phase)\n",
    "        ambient_wave = np.cos(step / 11.0 - phase)\n",
    "\n",
    "        gas_rate = 145.0 + 18.0 * load_wave + 4.0 * campaign_number\n",
    "        teg_rate = 4_800.0 + 520.0 * load_wave + 110.0 * ambient_wave\n",
    "        pressure = 119.0 + 2.8 * ambient_wave - 0.4 * campaign_number\n",
    "        water_34 = (\n",
    "            2.30\n",
    "            + 0.35 * load_wave\n",
    "            - 0.00018 * (teg_rate - 4_800.0)\n",
    "            + rng.normal(0.0, 0.035, len(step))\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        water_35 = (\n",
    "            2.22\n",
    "            + 0.23 * np.sin(step / 7.0 + phase + 0.5)\n",
    "            - 0.00010 * (teg_rate - 4_800.0)\n",
    "            + rng.normal(0.0, 0.035, len(step))\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "        frame = pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "            {\n",
    "                \"FieldName\": campaign_name,\n",
    "                \"time\": pd.date_range(\n",
    "                    \"2021-09-01\",\n",
    "                    periods=len(step),\n",
    "                    freq=\"30min\",\n",
    "                ),\n",
    "                \"AIT-1x34.PV\": water_34,\n",
    "                \"AIT-1x35.PV\": water_35,\n",
    "                \"STN1x-FT.INUSE2\": gas_rate,\n",
    "                \"FIT-1xx2.\": teg_rate,\n",
    "                \"PIT-xxx9.\": pressure,\n",
    "            }\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        frames.append(frame)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return pd.concat(frames, ignore_index=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "if USE_REMOTE_REPOSITORY_DATA:\n",
    "    with urlopen(DATA_URL, timeout=10) as response:\n",
    "        raw_datasets = pd.read_csv(BytesIO(response.read()))\n",
    "    data_resolution = \"public repository TimeSeries.csv\"\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    raw_datasets = build_deterministic_process_history()\n",
    "    data_resolution = \"deterministic documented fallback\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Data resolution: {data_resolution}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Raw rows: {len(raw_datasets)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "e0bad0c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Prepared rows: 96\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "selected_columns = [\n",
    "    \"FieldName\",\n",
    "    \"time\",\n",
    "    \"AIT-1x34.PV\",\n",
    "    \"AIT-1x35.PV\",\n",
    "    \"STN1x-FT.INUSE2\",\n",
    "    \"FIT-1xx2.\",\n",
    "    \"PIT-xxx9.\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "missing_columns = sorted(set(selected_columns) - set(raw_datasets.columns))\n",
    "assert not missing_columns, missing_columns\n",
    "\n",
    "row_stride = 10 if USE_REMOTE_REPOSITORY_DATA else 2\n",
    "datasets = raw_datasets.loc[:, selected_columns].iloc[::row_stride, :].copy()\n",
    "datasets = datasets[\n",
    "    datasets[\"AIT-1x35.PV\"].astype(float).abs() <= 30.0\n",
    "]\n",
    "datasets = datasets[\n",
    "    datasets[\"AIT-1x34.PV\"].astype(float).abs() <= 30.0\n",
    "]\n",
    "datasets = datasets.reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Prepared rows: {len(datasets)}\")"
   ]
  },
